            <div xml:id="d1322">

                <pb facs="1256" n="1090" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1090"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 151.07/84</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Secretary of War presents his compliments to the Honorable the Secretary of
                    State, and has the honor to inclose herewith with request for such action as may
                    be practicable, copy of telegram dated April 28, 1917, from the Commanding
                    General, Southern Department, Fort Sam Houston, Texas, in reply to telegram from
                    this Department of April 26, 1917, a copy of which is also inclosed, in regard
                    to the Chinese refugees now at Columbus, New Mexico. It is also requested that
                    this Department be informed as to the action of the Department of State in this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                                1917</hi></date>,</dateline>
                </closer>




